│ patch_name               │ robust_multiscale_tracker                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This design replaces the fixed moving-average approach with a causal robust               │
│                          │ local-polynomial measurement stage followed by an adaptive alpha-beta trend tracker.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The original programs use a fixed sliding mean or exponentially weighted mean. Those      │
│                          │ approaches reduce noise but introduce lag and can blur reversals or create false          │
│                          │ directional changes when volatility rises. The new method keeps the same input/output     │
│                          │ alignment—each output corresponds to the newest sample in its sliding window—but uses a   │
│                          │ fundamentally different estimation strategy:                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - A recency-weighted local quadratic regression estimates the signal at the current       │
│                          │ endpoint, avoiding the phase delay of centered smoothing.                                 │
│                          │ - Two Huber-style robust reweighting iterations suppress spikes and impulsive noise       │
│                          │ without treating them as genuine trend movement.                                          │
│                          │ - An adaptive alpha-beta state tracker combines position and slope estimates.             │
│                          │ - Innovation persistence increases responsiveness only when movement is directionally     │
│                          │ coherent across samples.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Isolated innovations receive less gain, reducing noise-induced slope changes and false  │
│                          │ reversals.                                                                                │
│                          │ - Adaptive innovation-scale estimation keeps the filter stable under non-stationary       │
│                          │ volatility.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This creates a low-lag, endpoint-aligned filter with explicit trend state, robust outlier │
│                          │ handling, and reversal-resistant adaptive smoothing.                                      │
