│ patch_name               │ adaptive_kalman_trend                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite replaces the enhanced exponential moving average with a robust adaptive      │
│                          │ constant-velocity Kalman filter. The filter jointly estimates signal level and local      │
│                          │ slope, allowing prediction to compensate for smoothing delay while suppressing            │
│                          │ high-frequency measurement noise.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Adaptive measurement-noise estimation responds to non-stationary volatility.            │
│                          │ - Innovation clipping prevents isolated outliers from creating false trend reversals.     │
│                          │ - Adaptive process noise increases responsiveness during persistent directional movement. │
│                          │ - State includes slope, improving trend tracking and reducing phase lag versus a moving   │
│                          │ average.                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Output remains causal and retains the original output alignment and length: `len(x) -   │
│                          │ window_size + 1`.                                                                         │
│                          │ - The basic algorithm remains available, but uses an efficient cumulative-sum moving      │
│                          │ average implementation.                                                                   │
