│ patch_name               │ confirmed_reversal_gate                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single-sample reversal suppression with a causal confirmation gate. The       │
│                          │ current gate can accept alternating medium-sized Kalman updates immediately, which still  │
│                          │ creates false reversals in volatile regions. The proposed edit keeps a pending            │
│                          │ opposite-direction displacement: a reversal is accepted when it is either clearly large   │
│                          │ relative to the adaptive noise scale or persists for two samples. This is a low-latency   │
│                          │ Schmitt-trigger/debounce mechanism. It reduces slope changes and false trend changes      │
│                          │ while allowing strong genuine turns through without an added confirmation delay. The gate │
│                          │ operates only on the reported trajectory and retains the Kalman state as the underlying   │
│                          │ predictor, avoiding the prior inconsistency caused by overwriting the Kalman level and    │
│                          │ slope after suppressing an output step.                                                   │
