│ patch_description        │ Add a two-sample directional confirmation gate to the causal Kalman tracker and reduce    │
│                          │ innovation-driven process-noise inflation. The current tracker is highly responsive but   │
│                          │ its process covariance grows sharply after individual noisy residuals, causing the        │
│                          │ estimated slope to change sign frequently (284 slope changes and 228 false reversals).    │
│                          │ The proposed gate preserves immediate response for substantial, coherent trend changes    │
│                          │ while holding only small first-sample opposite moves. A second consistent opposite        │
│                          │ increment, or an unusually large move, releases the gate. This hysteretic turn logic      │
│                          │ directly targets false reversals without adding a fixed moving-average delay. Reducing    │
│                          │ the adaptive process-noise coefficient also prevents isolated innovations from            │
│                          │ temporarily making the state estimate overly reactive.                                    │
