│ patch_name               │ hysteretic_output_trend                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Add a causal output hysteresis stage to the existing robust level-and-trend Kalman        │
│                          │ estimator. The filter state remains responsive, but the emitted value now requires short  │
│                          │ confirmation before accepting a change opposite to the established output direction. The  │
│                          │ adaptive deadband is derived from the current robust measurement-noise estimate, so it    │
│                          │ scales with volatility rather than using a fixed threshold.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly targets the largest weak metrics: noise-driven slope changes and false      │
│                          │ reversals. Continuing trends are emitted immediately, while genuine reversals are delayed │
│                          │ by at most one additional processed sample after exceeding the noise floor. This          │
│                          │ preserves low phase delay and tracking accuracy substantially better than increasing the  │
│                          │ Kalman smoothing globally.                                                                │
