│ patch_description        │ Replace the subtractive covariance update with the Joseph stabilized form. The current    │
│                          │ update can gradually lose positive-semidefiniteness through floating-point cancellation,  │
│                          │ especially when adaptive measurement and process variances change rapidly. Joseph form    │
│                          │ preserves covariance consistency, keeps Kalman gains stable, and permits the reversal     │
│                          │ gate to operate on a more reliable noise estimate. Explicit symmetrization and diagonal   │
│                          │ flooring prevent numerical degeneracy without changing the causal, low-latency            │
│                          │ architecture.                                                                             │
