│ patch_description        │ This rewrite replaces the fixed innovation clipping behavior with an adaptive robust      │
│                          │ innovation gate driven by an EWMA median-absolute-deviation-style scale estimate. The     │
│                          │ enhanced path uses a causal alpha-beta state tracker with:                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Robust clipping before both state correction and noise adaptation, preventing isolated  │
│                          │ spikes from corrupting level, slope, or future gain selection.                            │
│                          │ - Adaptive clipping thresholds bounded between conservative and permissive normalized     │
│                          │ innovation limits.                                                                        │
│                          │ - Gain scheduling based on clipped normalized innovation magnitude, improving response    │
│                          │ during persistent genuine transitions.                                                    │
│                          │ - Slope damping and bounded predictive lead to reduce lag without overshoot.              │
│                          │ - Directional hysteresis with confirmation for small reversals, reducing noise-induced    │
│                          │ slope changes and false reversals while allowing sufficiently large genuine reversals to  │
│                          │ pass immediately.                                                                         │
│                          │ - Preserved trailing-window output alignment, public functions, validation behavior,      │
│                          │ output lengths, and basic moving-average mode.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation remains single-pass, causal, NumPy-only, and efficient for real-time   │
│                          │ use.                                                                                      │
