│ patch_description        │ Replace the subtractive covariance update with the numerically robust Joseph form. The    │
│                          │ current `P - KHP` expression can gradually lose positive-semidefiniteness through         │
│                          │ floating-point cancellation, particularly when adaptive measurement/process variances     │
│                          │ produce aggressive gains. Joseph form preserves covariance consistency, while explicit    │
│                          │ symmetry restoration, variance floors, and cross-covariance bounding prevent invalid      │
│                          │ covariance states. This permits stable adaptive tracking without spurious gain excursions │
│                          │ that can cause false slope reversals.                                                     │
