│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ joseph_psd_covariance                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the subtractive covariance update with the numerically stable Joseph form. The    │
│                          │ current update can gradually lose covariance symmetry or positive-semidefiniteness under  │
│                          │ adaptive process noise and clipped innovations, producing erratic Kalman gains that       │
│                          │ manifest as noise-driven slope changes. The Joseph update preserves covariance structure, │
│                          │ explicitly symmetrizes the result, and applies small variance floors. This makes the      │
│                          │ adaptive tracker more stable during volatile regime changes while retaining its current   │
│                          │ low-lag state prediction and responsiveness.                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
