│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_kalman_consensus                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This revision replaces the expensive per-sample multiscale regression loop with a         │
│                          │ constant-time causal two-state Kalman tracker containing signal level and local slope.    │
│                          │ The process-noise schedule is bounded and innovation-adaptive: it remains low during      │
│                          │ quiet intervals for strong noise reduction, but increases during coherent deviations to   │
│                          │ reduce lag at genuine changes.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A lightweight output-direction controller applies a soft deadband and only delays weak    │
│                          │ counter-trend motion for one sample. Large reversals pass immediately, preserving         │
│                          │ responsiveness while reducing noise-induced slope changes and false reversals. The        │
│                          │ implementation retains the original public functions, validation behavior, output         │
│                          │ alignment, and output lengths.                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
