│ patch_name               │ dual_scale_trend_kalman                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The previous tracker used a single EWMA innovation scale (`scale_decay=0.955`) and fixed  │
│                          │ alpha-beta gain limits (`base_alpha=0.065`, `max_alpha=0.46`, `base_beta=0.004`,          │
│                          │ `max_beta=0.075`). This could either overreact to local noise or become too slow after    │
│                          │ volatility changes.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new enhanced implementation uses a causal dual-timescale robust noise estimator: a    │
│                          │ fast MAD estimate from recent first differences and a slow MAD estimate over the          │
│                          │ configured sliding-window span. Their bounded blend is smoothed gradually                 │
│                          │ (`noise_decay=0.965`) to prevent isolated spikes from changing gains. A gain-scheduled    │
│                          │ alpha-beta tracker uses increased gains only for persistent, clipped innovations. A       │
│                          │ volatility-scaled directional hysteresis gate suppresses small noise reversals while      │
│                          │ allowing larger genuine turns through immediately. The output alignment and public API    │
│                          │ remain unchanged: enhanced output starts at `window_size - 1` and has length `len(x) -    │
│                          │ window_size + 1`.                                                                         │
