│ patch_description        │ A low-latency adaptive constant-velocity Kalman tracker with robust innovation clipping,  │
│                          │ adaptive measurement-noise estimation, Joseph-form covariance stabilization, and          │
│                          │ output-level reversal hysteresis.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Compared with repeated multi-window regression, this implementation is O(n),              │
│                          │ substantially reducing execution latency. The Kalman state tracks both level and slope,   │
│                          │ allowing prompt response to genuine movement. Innovation-dependent process noise          │
│                          │ increases agility during coherent transitions, while robust residual scaling and bounded  │
│                          │ innovations prevent isolated spikes from destabilizing the estimate. A two-sample,        │
│                          │ displacement-aware reversal gate is applied only to the displayed output, reducing        │
│                          │ noise-induced directional changes without preventing the underlying tracker from learning │
│                          │ a real turn immediately.                                                                  │
