│ patch_description        │ Replace the single-sample directional deadband with a low-latency persistence gate. The   │
│                          │ current filter accepts many opposite-direction increments once they exceed a relatively   │
│                          │ small threshold, which explains the high slope-change and false-reversal counts. The new  │
│                          │ gate requires two consecutive opposing moves whose accumulated displacement is meaningful │
│                          │ relative to the adaptive noise scale, while allowing a sufficiently strong turn to pass   │
│                          │ immediately. Unconfirmed opposing samples hold the output level and strongly attenuate    │
│                          │ slope, preserving the existing filter’s fast consensus dynamics while reducing            │
│                          │ noise-induced directional flicker. This targets false reversals and slope changes with    │
│                          │ only a one-sample confirmation cost for ordinary genuine reversals.                       │
