│ patch_name               │ distance_confirmed_reversal_gate                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the output-only reversal gate without changing the responsive alpha-beta core. │
│                          │ The existing counter requires only sample count after a candidate crosses the small band; │
│                          │ it can therefore accept repeated weak noise excursions. This edit adds a                  │
│                          │ volatility-normalized excursion requirement, raises the immediate-turn threshold, and     │
│                          │ removes the unconfirmed large-delta bypass. A genuine turn can still pass rapidly when    │
│                          │ the dual-scale slope model agrees, while weak counter-moves need both persistence and     │
│                          │ sufficient displacement. This should reduce false reversals and slope changes with only   │
│                          │ limited additional lag.                                                                   │
