│ patch_description        │ Add a causal, confidence-scaled reversal confirmation stage to the emitted output. The    │
│                          │ Kalman state remains responsive and continues to assimilate every robustly clipped        │
│                          │ observation, but a directional change in the published signal now requires two            │
│                          │ consecutive noise-significant estimates. This separates state tracking from trend         │
│                          │ declaration: isolated innovations and short-window contamination no longer immediately    │
│                          │ create an output turn, while sustained genuine reversals incur only one-sample            │
│                          │ confirmation latency. The threshold scales with the learned residual noise level,         │
│                          │ preserving sensitivity during quiet periods and avoiding excessive false-reversal         │
│                          │ suppression in volatile regions.                                                          │
