│ patch_description        │ Make the fast directional model influential only when its recent difference-noise         │
│                          │ estimate and newest residual indicate that it is reliable. The current fixed 0.55         │
│                          │ fast-slope consensus can allow a short noisy interval or endpoint impulse to affect the   │
│                          │ candidate lead and reversal confirmation. This edit records fast/slow robust scales,      │
│                          │ derives an impulse/recent-volatility reliability factor, and reduces fast-model influence │
│                          │ unless there is meaningful directional activity with a stable short-horizon fit. The slow │
│                          │ model remains dominant during contaminated intervals, reducing false reversals and slope  │
│                          │ changes, while the fast model still receives additional weight during clean, active turns │
│                          │ to preserve low lag.                                                                      │
