│                          │ current implementation only delays opposite increments smaller than the reversal band, so │
│                          │ moderately large noise-driven endpoint movements can immediately flip direction. This     │
│                          │ edit gates every opposing movement unless it has strong fast/slow slope consensus, or     │
│                          │ exceptionally strong fast consensus, while retaining a two-sample                         │
│                          │ accumulated-displacement fallback for genuine turns whose slow model has not yet rotated. │
│                          │ This should substantially reduce slope changes and false reversals while limiting added   │
│                          │ turn lag.                                                                                 │
