│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the alpha-beta state tracker with a causal robust            │
│                          │ multi-scale local-regression filter. At each sample it fits both short-horizon and        │
│                          │ long-horizon exponentially weighted local linear models over the trailing window. Huber   │
│                          │ reweighting suppresses impulses, while model residual scales determine whether the        │
│                          │ responsive short model is trustworthy enough to influence the output. The fitted endpoint │
│                          │ estimates provide substantially less phase delay than a trailing average, and a           │
│                          │ slope-consensus reversal gate suppresses noise-driven directional changes without         │
│                          │ preventing sustained real turns. The approach uses sliding robust regression rather than  │
│                          │ recursive state estimation, making it fundamentally different from the prior tracker.     │
