│ patch_name               │ slope_confirmed_reversals                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Make reversal acceptance depend on the reliability of the estimated directional state,    │
│                          │ not solely on two endpoint displacements. The current gate treats two opposite output     │
│                          │ candidates as sufficient even when the Kalman slope still indicates the previous trend,   │
│                          │ allowing short-lived noisy excursions to create false reversals. This edit accepts a      │
│                          │ large reversal promptly only when both the accumulated endpoint displacement and internal │
│                          │ slope agree. Weak or slope-inconsistent reversals require one additional persistent       │
│                          │ sample. This should reduce slope changes and false reversals while retaining low lag for  │
│                          │ decisive genuine turns.                                                                   │
