│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Uses robust fast/slow exponentially weighted slope models with volatility-aware         │
│                          │ blending.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Explicitly reduces fast-model influence when short-term fit noise or endpoint residuals │
│                          │ indicate impulse contamination.                                                           │
│                          │ - Adds innovation reliability weighting so isolated outliers cannot trigger excessive     │
│                          │ level/slope response.                                                                     │
│                          │ - Uses adaptive prediction lead: it is increased for coherent trends and reduced during   │
│                          │ local volatility bursts.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Strengthens reversal confirmation through multi-sample directional evidence, slope      │
│                          │ agreement, and adaptive deadbands.                                                        │
│                          │ - Keeps causal operation, bounded memory, and low computational cost per sample.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The basic moving-average mode is unchanged.                                               │
