│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ robust_multiscale_trendgate                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the state-space Kalman approach with a causal multiscale     │
│                          │ robust-regression filter. At each trailing-window endpoint it fits both a slow and a fast │
│                          │ exponentially weighted local-linear model using Huber reweighting. The slow model         │
│                          │ supplies stable denoising, while the fast model supplies low-lag response to genuine      │
│                          │ changes.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The models are blended only when the fast fit is reliable: its residual scale, endpoint   │
│                          │ residual, and agreement with the slow slope determine its influence. A final causal trend │
│                          │ gate attenuates only weak counter-direction movements, reducing noise-induced reversals   │
│                          │ without preventing sustained trend changes. The algorithm preserves the original          │
│                          │ input/output API and trailing-window output alignment.                                    │
