│ patch_description        │ Gate pending reversal accumulation with directional slope evidence and decay weak         │
│                          │ evidence instead of treating every opposite endpoint step as confirmation. The current    │
│                          │ persistence branch can accept a reversal after two opposite candidate steps even when the │
│                          │ fast/consensus trend models do not support that direction, which explains excess false    │
│                          │ reversals. This change retains the immediate low-lag path for strongly model-confirmed    │
│                          │ turns, while requiring persistent turns to show at least partial fast or consensus slope  │
│                          │ support. Weak or alternating endpoint noise now decays pending distance/count, preventing │
│                          │ stale evidence from accumulating into a false directional change.                         │
