│ patch_name               │ turn_aware_predictive_lead                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded, turn-aware predictive lead to the published level. The Kalman level is     │
│                          │ intentionally smoothed and consequently retains some residual lag during sustained        │
│                          │ coherent motion. A small extrapolation based on consensus between the instantaneous       │
│                          │ Kalman slope and the smoothed recent increment improves tracking responsiveness without   │
│                          │ changing the causal estimator.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The lead is disabled when the two slope estimates disagree, reduced during deceleration,  │
│                          │ and attenuated when the innovation persistently opposes the current trend. These          │
│                          │ conditions commonly precede genuine turns, so suppressing prediction there avoids         │
│                          │ overshoot and the subsequent noise-induced counter-reversal. The lead is also bounded     │
│                          │ relative to the adaptive noise scale, preserving robust behavior during volatile regimes. │
